input_only: False
instruction: 'Provide a variety of cooking methods such as grilling, stewing, sautéing or roasting within the beef recipes for weeknight dinners. In addition, include recipes that are appropriate for different levels of cooking experience, and indicate the approximate cooking times for each recipe. Consider including dishes that can be made in advance, making it easier for those with busy schedules to have dinner ready quickly. Finally, be sure to note any dietary restrictions or allergies the recipes may be suitable for.'
target: '1. Grilled Flank Steak with Chimichurri Sauce - for experienced cooks\n- Preheat grill to high heat (approx. 400°F)\n- Season 1 lb. Flank steak with salt and pepper\n- Grill for 5-7 minutes per side for medium-rare\n- Let rest for 5-10 minutes before slicing against the grain\n- For the chimichurri sauce, blend together 1/2 cup fresh parsley, 1/2 cup fresh cilantro, 3 garlic cloves, 1/4 cup red wine vinegar, 1 tsp. Red pepper flakes, 1 tsp. Salt, and 1/2 cup olive oil\n- Serve steak with sauce\n\nApprox. Cooking time: 15-20 minutes\n\nSuitable for: gluten-free, dairy-free, paleo, Whole30\n\n2. Slow Cooker Beef Stew - for beginners\n- In a slow cooker, combine 2 lbs. Cubed beef stew meat, 1 diced onion, 4 diced carrots, 4 diced celery stalks, 3 minced garlic cloves, 1 bay leaf, 1 tsp. Dried thyme, 1 tsp. Salt, and 1/2 tsp. Black pepper\n- Pour in 4 cups beef broth and 2 cups diced potatoes\n- Cook on low for 8 hours or high for 4 hours\n- Remove bay leaf before serving\n\nApprox. Cooking time: 4-8 hours\n\nSuitable for: gluten-free, dairy-free\n\n3. Sautéed Beef and Broccoli Stir-Fry - for intermediate cooks\n- In a large skillet, heat 1 tbsp. Vegetable oil over medium-high heat\n- Sauté 1 lb. Thinly sliced beef sirloin until browned, then remove from skillet and set aside\n- In the same skillet, add 1 chopped onion and 2 minced garlic cloves, sauté for 2-3 minutes until onion is translucent\n- Add 4 cups broccoli florets and 1 sliced bell pepper, sauté for 2-3 minutes\n- Stir in 1/4 cup soy sauce, 2 tbsp. Hoisin sauce, and 1 tbsp. Honey\n- Add beef back to the skillet and heat for 1-2 minutes until sauce is bubbly\n\nApprox. Cooking time: 20-25 minutes\n\nSuitable for: dairy-free\n\n4. Herb-Roasted Beef Tenderloin - for experienced cooks\n- Preheat oven to 425°F\n- In a small bowl, mix together 2 tbsp. Fresh thyme, 2 tbsp. Fresh rosemary, 2 minced garlic cloves, 1 tbsp. Olive oil, 1 tsp. Salt, and 1/2 tsp. Black pepper\n- Rub mixture all over a 2 lb. Beef tenderloin roast\n- Roast in the oven for 30-40 minutes, until internal temperature reaches 130°F for medium-rare\n- Let rest for 10-15 minutes before slicing\n\nApprox. Cooking time: 40-55 minutes\n\nSuitable for: gluten-free, dairy-free, paleo, Whole30\n\n5. Slow Cooker Italian Beef Sandwiches - for beginners\n- In a slow cooker, combine 2 lbs. Beef chuck roast, 1 diced onion, 3 minced garlic cloves, 1 tbsp. Italian seasoning, 1 tsp. Salt, and 1/2 tsp. Black pepper\n- Pour in 1 cup beef broth and 1/2 cup pepperoncini juice\n- Cook on low for 8 hours or high for 4 hours\n- Remove beef and shred with two forks\n- Serve on hoagie rolls with additional pepperoncini peppers and provolone cheese, if desired\n\nApprox. Cooking time: 4-8 hours\n\nSuitable for: dairy-free'
formatted_prompt: '<|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\nProvide a variety of cooking methods such as grilling, stewing, sautéing or roasting within the beef recipes for weeknight dinners. In addition, include recipes that are appropriate for different levels of cooking experience, and indicate the approximate cooking times for each recipe. Consider including dishes that can be made in advance, making it easier for those with busy schedules to have dinner ready quickly. Finally, be sure to note any dietary restrictions or allergies the recipes may be suitable for.<|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n1. Grilled Flank Steak with Chimichurri Sauce - for experienced cooks\n- Preheat grill to high heat (approx. 400°F)\n- Season 1 lb. Flank steak with salt and pepper\n- Grill for 5-7 minutes per side for medium-rare\n- Let rest for 5-10 minutes before slicing against the grain\n- For the chimichurri sauce, blend together 1/2 cup fresh parsley, 1/2 cup fresh cilantro, 3 garlic cloves, 1/4 cup red wine vinegar, 1 tsp. Red pepper flakes, 1 tsp. Salt, and 1/2 cup olive oil\n- Serve steak with sauce\n\nApprox. Cooking time: 15-20 minutes\n\nSuitable for: gluten-free, dairy-free, paleo, Whole30\n\n2. Slow Cooker Beef Stew - for beginners\n- In a slow cooker, combine 2 lbs. Cubed beef stew meat, 1 diced onion, 4 diced carrots, 4 diced celery stalks, 3 minced garlic cloves, 1 bay leaf, 1 tsp. Dried thyme, 1 tsp. Salt, and 1/2 tsp. Black pepper\n- Pour in 4 cups beef broth and 2 cups diced potatoes\n- Cook on low for 8 hours or high for 4 hours\n- Remove bay leaf before serving\n\nApprox. Cooking time: 4-8 hours\n\nSuitable for: gluten-free, dairy-free\n\n3. Sautéed Beef and Broccoli Stir-Fry - for intermediate cooks\n- In a large skillet, heat 1 tbsp. Vegetable oil over medium-high heat\n- Sauté 1 lb. Thinly sliced beef sirloin until browned, then remove from skillet and set aside\n- In the same skillet, add 1 chopped onion and 2 minced garlic cloves, sauté for 2-3 minutes until onion is translucent\n- Add 4 cups broccoli florets and 1 sliced bell pepper, sauté for 2-3 minutes\n- Stir in 1/4 cup soy sauce, 2 tbsp. Hoisin sauce, and 1 tbsp. Honey\n- Add beef back to the skillet and heat for 1-2 minutes until sauce is bubbly\n\nApprox. Cooking time: 20-25 minutes\n\nSuitable for: dairy-free\n\n4. Herb-Roasted Beef Tenderloin - for experienced cooks\n- Preheat oven to 425°F\n- In a small bowl, mix together 2 tbsp. Fresh thyme, 2 tbsp. Fresh rosemary, 2 minced garlic cloves, 1 tbsp. Olive oil, 1 tsp. Salt, and 1/2 tsp. Black pepper\n- Rub mixture all over a 2 lb. Beef tenderloin roast\n- Roast in the oven for 30-40 minutes, until internal temperature reaches 130°F for medium-rare\n- Let rest for 10-15 minutes before slicing\n\nApprox. Cooking time: 40-55 minutes\n\nSuitable for: gluten-free, dairy-free, paleo, Whole30\n\n5. Slow Cooker Italian Beef Sandwiches - for beginners\n- In a slow cooker, combine 2 lbs. Beef chuck roast, 1 diced onion, 3 minced garlic cloves, 1 tbsp. Italian seasoning, 1 tsp. Salt, and 1/2 tsp. Black pepper\n- Pour in 1 cup beef broth and 1/2 cup pepperoncini juice\n- Cook on low for 8 hours or high for 4 hours\n- Remove beef and shred with two forks\n- Serve on hoagie rolls with additional pepperoncini peppers and provolone cheese, if desired\n\nApprox. Cooking time: 4-8 hours\n\nSuitable for: dairy-free<|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\nCan you suggest any side dish options that would complement these beef dishes? Something easy to make would be ideal.<|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\nAbsolutely! Here are some easy side dish options that would complement these beef dishes:\n\n1. Grilled Asparagus - Toss asparagus spears in olive oil and season with salt and pepper. Grill over high heat for about 5 minutes, or until tender and slightly charred. 2. Roasted Garlic Mashed Potatoes - Boil peeled and cubed potatoes until tender, then drain and mash with butter, milk, roasted garlic, and salt and pepper to taste. 3. Simple Side Salad - Toss mixed greens with a simple vinaigrette made from olive oil, balsamic vinegar, Dijon mustard, and honey. 4. Roasted Veggies - Toss your choice of veggies (such as carrots, bell peppers, mushrooms, or zucchini) in olive oil and season with salt and pepper. Roast in the oven at 400°F for about 20-25 minutes, or until tender and slightly caramelized. 5. Garlic Bread - Slice a baguette in half lengthwise and spread garlic butter on each half. Toast in the oven at 400°F for about 5-7 minutes, or until crispy and golden brown. Hope you find these suggestions helpful!<|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\nCan you also recommend some dessert options that would pair well with these beef dishes? Something quick and easy to make would be great.<|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\nOf course! Here are some quick and easy dessert options that pair well with beef dishes:\n\n1. Chocolate Mousse - Beat heavy cream until stiff peaks form, then fold in melted chocolate and a pinch of salt. Chill in the refrigerator for at least 2 hours before serving. 2. Apple Crisp - Mix sliced apples with cinnamon, brown sugar, and a squeeze of lemon juice, then top with a mixture of oats, flour, brown sugar, and melted butter. Bake in the oven at 375°F for about 30-35 minutes, or until the topping is golden brown. 3. Vanilla Ice Cream with Caramel Sauce - Serve a scoop of vanilla ice cream with a drizzle of homemade or store-bought caramel sauce. 4. Berry Pudding - Mix cooked and pureed berries with sugar, cornstarch, and lemon juice, then chill until set to form a pudding-like consistency. Serve with a dollop of whipped cream. 5. Brownies - Whip up a batch of chocolate brownies and serve warm with a scoop of vanilla ice cream on top. Hope you enjoy these dessert suggestions!'
